 - Internal Noctalia notifications (shell and plugins) are toast-only and are not stored in notification history, except [calendar reminders](/noctalia/services/calendar/#reminders).
 - Notification summaries are always plain text. Noctalia does not advertise body-markup support, so it strips the standard notification body tags (`b`, `i`, `u`, `a`, `img`, `br`) while preserving malformed or unsupported angle-bracket text literally. A `br` tag becomes a line break.
 - By default, dismissing a toast (right-click, close button, or `noctalia msg notification-clear-active`) only hides it. The entry stays in control-center history and still counts as unread until the notifications tab is opened. Set `keep_dismissed_in_history = false` to remove the history entry when its toast is dismissed. Timed-out notifications remain in history.
+- `hide_content = true` keeps what a notification says off the screen and out of history: a notification from an app, or a calendar reminder, that arrives while it is on is shown and stored with its sender and the summary "Notification", with no body and no image; an icon that is a file is dropped too. Its actions still work, and filters still match the real text. Notifications that arrived before it was turned on are left as they were, and what is withheld is not kept anywhere, so turning it off does not bring it back. Internal Noctalia toasts are not changed.
 - When the sending app withdraws a notification itself (for example a chat app once the message has been read there), its history entry is kept but no longer counts as unread.
 - `history_retention_hours` removes stored notifications older than the configured number of hours. The default `0` retains history indefinitely; accepted values are `0`–`8760`.
 - `collapse_on_dismiss = true` (default) causes remaining toasts to slide into a compact stack when one is dismissed. Set to `false` for stable-slot behavior where toasts keep their original positions.
